{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c595","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aa0a-86a0-7111-8cdf-bab999a2f9d6"},"sequence":293,"recorded_at":1780531400000581,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"03f62105-9a02-4d8f-abd9-d3525c9bfed8","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"03f62105-9a02-4d8f-abd9-d3525c9bfed8","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"03f62105-9a02-4d8f-abd9-d3525c9bfed8"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0aa0b-5087-76c0-a1c5-a605460c4616"},"task_id":"01a0aa0b-5087-76c0-a1c5-a605460c4616","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0aa0b-5087-76c0-a1c5-a605460c4616","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/r5-outcome.md`.\n1|# TASK-260916-304bw2 — R5 final boundary and cleanup (developer outcome)\n2|\n3|Status: ready for review (board `to-review`).\n4|\n5|Revision 5 repairs the two concrete residual defects from rev4 and nothing\n6|else. It adopts both exact rev4 reviewer probes as maintained\n7|production-entry regressions, enforces the initiating-session authority\n8|after the final stopped inspection AND at the actual installer mutation\n9|boundary, and gives Load/Apply owner/generation-bound cleanup that\n10|releases the busy state on invalidation without letting an old operation\n11|clear a newer one. Accepted R4 incarnation/editor-identity fixes,\n12|installer-wide lease, stopped-only unregister, distinct service\n13|identities, fail-closed persistence, corrected real login policy, and the\n14|repository editor are preserved. No production runner was stopped,\n15|re-registered, or interrupted; the candidate is left UNCOMMITTED in the\n16|Story worktree.\n17|\n18|## Fixes by finding\n19|\n20|### R4-F1 — initiating-session authority through the final inspection\n21|- `Runners.Flow.runUnregister`: after the final `requireConfirmedStopped`\n22|  (which awaits production launchctl), re-checks catalog generation and\n23|  `sessionStill(startedIdentity)` before invoking the installer.\n24|- `RunnerInstallerService.unregister(directory:removeToken:sessionAuthority:)`:\n25|  new optional authority closure, enforced after the installer-wide lease\n26|  is held and immediately before `config.sh remove` begins. On failure it\n27|  throws the new `RegistrationError.sessionInvalidated`; the lease\n28|  releases via `defer`, the Flow catch suppresses publication (session\n29|  changed), and the unregister epilogue releases the operation state so an\n30|  explicit retry stays possible.\n31|- `Runners.Flow.sessionMatches` (new, nonisolated): pure incarnation\n32|  comparison shared by `sessionStill` and the installer-boundary closure,\n33|  so both enforce identical authority without capturing the Flow actor.\n34|\n35|### R4-F2 — owner/generation-bound Load/Apply cleanup\n36|- `Runners.Flow.groupAccessGeneration` (new): every Load/Apply takes the\n37|  next per-editor operation number before publishing its loading state.\n38|- `publishGroupAccessIfCurrent`: success/error/invalidation publications\n39|  land only when the operation still owns the editor; a superseded\n40|  completion publishes nothing — no cleared busy state, no stale data.\n41|- `releaseGroupAccessAfterSessionChange`: session invalidation publishes\n42|  an explicit retry message (\"GitHub session changed during group\n43|  access. Reload group access to retry in the current session.\") instead\n44|  of wedging on a spinner. Applied at every session guard and in the\n45|  error path's session-changed branch, in both Load and Apply.\n46|- `abandonGroupAccessAfterCatalogChange`: catalog-stale completions\n47|  release only when the entry still exists and no explicit invalidation\n48|  already released it (removal prunes; relink invalidates).\n49|- `removeFromApp`/`relink` drop the editor's operation ownership, so an\n50|  in-flight op can neither publish into nor release the editor after the\n51|  entry is removed or relinked (covers the remove-then-re-add edge).\n52|- `consumeStoredEditorAuthority` takes the operation and gates its\n53|  mismatch invalidation on ownership.\n54|\n55|## Production call sites\n56|\n57|| Fix | Call site |\n58||---|---|\n59|| R4-F1 | `Runners.Flow.apply(.unregister)` → `runUnregister` post-final-inspection `sessionStill` → `RunnerInstallerService.unregister(sessionAuthority:)` before `config.sh remove` |\n60|| R4-F2 | `Runners.Flow.apply(.loadGroupAccess/.applyGroupAccess)` → `beginGroupAccessOperation` → `release/abandon/publish…IfCurrent` → `Runners.Action.groupAccessFailed/Loaded` |\n61|\n62|## Tests: 5 new + 2 adopted probes (6 scenarios), 229 total green\n63|\n64|Adopted probes (failed exit 1 with 4 issues on rev4, pass now):\n65|`reviewR4LogoutDuringFinalStoppedInspectionMustRefuseRemoval`,\n66|`reviewR4SessionInvalidationMustReleaseEditorLoading(apply:)` (both cases).\n67|\n68|New bounds:\n69|`unregisterRefusesLogoutBetweenFinalInspectionAndConfigRemove`\n70|(installer-boundary refusal via deterministic flip order + same-Flow\n71|retry succeeds), `editorOverlappingLoadSuppressesStaleCompletion`\n72|(latched same-Flow overlap, stale completion suppressed, newer data\n73|intact, through the production reducer + refresh),\n74|`editorRetryAfterSessionInvalidationSucceedsOnSameFlow` (released editor\n75|retried in the new session on the same Flow, through the reducer).\n76|\n77|Updated contract (4 tests): session-invalidated Load/Apply now publishes\n78|the named cleanup message instead of staying silent —\n79|`applyGroupAccessStopsWhenSessionChangesMidApply`,\n80|`applyGroupAccessStopsWhenServerSwitchesMidApply`,\n81|`loadGroupAccessStopsPublishingAfterMidLoadLogout`,\n82|`reviewR3SiblingLoadDuringReloginMustNotPublishAccess`. Safety assertions\n83|(no PUT, no Loaded, exact request counts) are unchanged; only the\n84|wedging `error == nil` expectation became the explicit-cleanup assertion.\n85|\n86|Existing positive/new-session controls reused and green:\n87|`unregisterRemovesRemoteKeepsFilesAndEntry`,\n88|`unregisterRetryInNewIncarnationSucceeds`,\n89|`unregisterReleasesOperationStateAfterSessionLoss`,\n90|`applySucceedsAfterTokenRefreshWithinSameLogin`.\n91|\n92|AC coverage: 18 of 19 named rows driven through production entry points\n93|(unchanged from R4; row 18, full UI paths, remains the stated manual-UI\n94|bound — no UI tests per task). R5 findings touched rows 11/16 and the\n95|async ownership/retry contract.\n96|\n97|## Mutant evidence: 3 narrowing, 0 survivors\n98|\n99|Tree reverted after each run (diff-verified byte-identical to the\n100|pre-mutant backup); focused suite re-run green afterwards. Each mutant\n101|keeps the gate present and weakens it to admit exactly one rejected\n102|subclass; a retained-gate control still passes in the same run.\n103|\n104|| Mutant | Narrows the gate to | Named failing test | Exit |\n105||---|---|---|---|\n106|| `unregister-admits-final-inspection-invalidation` | Unregister keeps pre-inspection/token/stopped gates, admits session invalidation between final stopped inspection and config.sh remove (Flow post-inspection check + installer enforcement omitted) | `reviewR4LogoutDuringFinalStoppedInspectionMustRefuseRemoval` (2 issues: installer ran + ID cleared); `unregisterRefusesLogoutBetweenFinalInspectionAndConfigRemove` (3 issues); `unregisterRefusesRunningService`, `unregisterRevalidatesStoppedAtSideEffectBoundary`, `unregisterRemovesRemoteKeepsFilesAndEntry` still pass | 1 |\n107|| `load-omits-invalidation-cleanup` | Load keeps success/error publication + ownership gating + Apply cleanup, omits session-invalidation cleanup on Load (3 guards + error branch) | `reviewR4SessionInvalidationMustReleaseEditorLoading(apply:false)` (loading stuck); `loadGroupAccessStopsPublishingAfterMidLoadLogout` (no cleanup); F2(apply:true) + `reviewR3SameAccountReloginDuringPut` still pass | 1 |\n108|| `apply-omits-invalidation-cleanup` | Apply keeps success/error publication + ownership gating + Load cleanup, omits session-invalidation cleanup on Apply (4 guards + error branch) | `reviewR4SessionInvalidationMustReleaseEditorLoading(apply:true)` (loading stuck); `applyGroupAccessStopsWhenSessionChangesMidApply` (no cleanup); F2(apply:false) + `reviewR3SiblingLoad` still pass | 1 |\n109|\n110|No survivors. No delete-only rows claimed as narrowing.\n111|\n112|## Validation (real exit codes)\n113|\n114|- `swift test --package-path Packages/RunnerControlCore` → exit 0, 229\n115|  tests passed (224 R4 + 5 R5), re-run green after mutant reverts. One\n116|  earlier full run showed a single non-reproducing issue; three\n117|  consecutive full runs since are green, and the three new tests pass 3/3\n118|  in isolation.\n119|- `python3 -m unittest discover -s Scripts/tests` → exit 0, 62 tests OK\n120|  (release machinery untouched).\n121|- `./Scripts/build.sh` → exit 0, `BUILD SUCCEEDED`;\n122|  `codesign --verify --deep --strict` → exit 0;\n123|  `1.2.0`, `works.relux.runnercontrol`, TeamIdentifier `262RZ595FP`,\n124|  fresh candidate in `.temp/products/` (signed 2026-09-16 15:37 UTC).\n125|- No configured linter (no SwiftLint config); build shows no new\n126|  warnings in changed files.\n127|- Production (read-only): both runners live (exactly one `runsvc.sh` +\n128|  one `Runner.Listener` each for macbook-iv and cocoaskills); no\n129|  `actions.runner.*` in `~/Library/LaunchAgents` (manual external login\n130|  OFF preserved). No production state changed.\n131|\n132|## Stated bounds\n133|\n134|- UI confirmation paths are manual (root CUA on the fresh candidate; no\n135|  UI tests per task). The production Flow gates behind them are covered.\n136|- Overlap ownership is per Flow instance; production composes exactly one\n137|  `Runners.Flow` per runtime, so cross-Flow overlap cannot arise outside\n138|  tests that deliberately build two Flows.\n139|- An in-flight membership page loop may finish its current read after a\n140|  mid-loop login replacement; no write, confirmation read, or publication\n141|  follows (R4 bound, unchanged).\n142|- A remove token minted just before a session invalidation expires\n143|  unused; the refused side effect is `config.sh remove` (proven\n144|  installer-idle, now at two boundary points).\n145|- Catalog entries without a recorded server/scope predate the original\n146|  binding and rely on disk-vs-session checks for relink (R4 bound,\n147|  unchanged).","final_result":true}}}
